    "updated_at": "2026-09-08T12:56:22Z",
    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #337\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-131-approval-baseline-02-03-decide-and-exe-thr_ndnryk2hej` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #131: decide and execute approval requests atomically.\n\n- Authenticated-user approve/reject via `decideApprovalRequest`, one atomic `UPDATE ... WHERE status='pending'`. Rejection creates no job; approval enqueues the reserved `approvalExecute` job in the same transaction.\n- The job handler (`handleApprovalRequestExecuteTask`) atomically claims execution (`UPDATE ... WHERE executed_at IS NULL`), reloads the stored payload, and performs only the deferred choke-point call — no `AgentSession`, no conversation reconstruction, no mutation of the originating run.\n- Outcome (`executedAt`/`executionError`/`executionResult`) is recorded directly on `approval_requests` (additive migration `0022`), following the \"no second log table\" convention — the table itself is the audit trail.\n- Both atomic UPDATEs are documented as the single-attempt baseline that #89 can later upgrade to full exactly-once transaction semantics without altering the user-facing state machine.\n- New `PATCH /api/approval-requests/:id` HTTP endpoint treats repeated decisions as deterministic 200 no-ops rather than errors.\n\nVerified: full unit (83), integration (641), and e2e (5) test suites pass; all packages build cleanly with `tsc`; zero ESLint errors; Prettier clean on all touched files.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
